<article class="env-lemma" id="00XY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00XY">Lemma <span data-tag="00XY">7.22.2</span>.</a> Notation and assumptions as in Lemma <a href="/tag/00XX" data-tag="00XX">7.22.1</a>. If in addition $v$ is continuous then $v$ defines a morphism of sites $f : \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{D}$ whose associated morphism of topoi is equal to $g$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      We will use the results of Lemma <a href="/tag/00XX" data-tag="00XX">7.22.1</a> without further mention. To prove that $v$ defines a morphism of sites $f$ as in the statement of the lemma, we have to show that $v_ s$ is an exact functor (see Definition <a href="/tag/00X1" data-tag="00X1">7.14.1</a>). Since $v_ s\mathcal{G} = (v_ p\mathcal{G})^\#  = g^{-1}\mathcal{G}$ this follows from the fact that $g$ is a morphism of topoi. Then we see that $f^{-1} = v_ s = g^{-1}$ and we find that $f = g$ as morphisms of topoi. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>